; Coverage scope for the 80% gate (see config/pytest.ini's --cov-fail-under).
;
; All three tiers are now implemented and tested, so every framework counts
; against the gate like any other real code. Nothing is omitted for being
; "not written yet" any more.
;
; The one remaining omission is cockpit/testing/*, which is testing
; infrastructure and example code (fixtures, demo unit/integration/benchmark
; modules) rather than application logic -- pytest actually collects and runs
; those demo modules as tests, so measuring their coverage would be circular.
[run]
omit =
    cockpit/testing/*
